# Codice Perfetto (code craftsmanship)

## Ponytail (lazy senior)

Pick the simplest solution that works. Stop at the first rung that holds: YAGNI → stdlib → platform → installed dependency → one-liner → minimum code.

- No unrequested abstractions, dependencies, or boilerplate.
- Deletion over addition. Boring over clever. Fewest files possible.
- Mark intentional shortcuts with a `ponytail:` comment that names the ceiling and upgrade path.
- Not lazy about: trust-boundary validation, data-loss prevention, security, accessibility, hardware calibration, anything explicitly requested.
- Non-trivial logic leaves ONE runnable check behind.

## Descriptive names (zero abbreviations)

- Full words only (`$authenticatedUser`, `$collectionFieldDefinition`). No `cfg`/`res`/`req`/`val`/`ctx`/`idx`.
- Loop indices `i`/`j`/`k` only in tight numeric loops.
- Booleans and boolean methods: prefix `is` / `has` / `can` / `should` — except Laravel contract method names (`authorize`, Policy `view`/`create`/`update`/`delete`, `passes`, `broadcastWhen`) and native HTML/React/Radix/shadcn/Inertia boolean props (`disabled`, `required`, `checked`, `open`, `asChild`, `preserveScroll`, …).
- Collections: specific plurals or explicit map names — never `$data` / `$list`.

## Explicit role suffixes (custom code only)

Only Eloquent Models use bare domain nouns. Every other custom class ends with its role: `Controller`, `Request`, `Resource`, `Response`, `Middleware`, `Policy`, `Job`, `Command`, `Event`, `Listener`, `Notification`, `Enum`, `Action` (single `execute(...)`), `Service`, `Data` (`readonly`), `Trait`, `Builder`, `Observer`, `Rule`, `Exception`.

**Never rename** Laravel / Fortify / starter-kit scaffolding or vendor-published / shadcn files. Exempt via Pest `->ignoring(...)` in `tests/Arch/NamingArchitectureTest.php`.

## 5 Enterprise Laravel architecture pillars

1. Thin controllers: Request → Action/Service (+ `*Data` DTO) → Resource/Inertia. No `DB` facade in controllers.
2. Domain boundaries: `app/Actions` (writes), `app/Services` (orchestration/reads/integrations), `app/Data` (readonly DTOs), `app/Traits`.
3. Clean models: relationships, casts, scopes, constants only.
4. Centralized authorization in `app/Policies`.
5. Pest Arch guardrails in CI (`NamingArchitectureTest`).

## Documentation

Supersedes “comments only for exceptionally complex logic”.

- English PHPDoc / JSDoc on classes, components, hooks, and non-trivial methods.
- Document array shapes, side effects, invariants, `@throws` — not line-by-line noise.
- Explicit curly braces; blank lines around control-flow blocks; strict DRY.

## Immutable contracts

- Never edit committed `database/migrations/` — forward-only new migrations only.
- Preserve enum backing values, `broadcastAs()` names, JSON keys, route names, Inertia page paths.
